1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,440
I can change for the better. I know I can.

2
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,860
I can be someone who makes a difference.

3
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,940
Do you think you can save her?

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:50,480
What have I done?

5
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:53,080
We... what have we done?

6
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:54,460
No!

7
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:35,780
Back up. You just told us Iroha was missing? When did that happen?

8
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:43,060
Please, Mifuyu. If you know anything about Iroha or the Magius' plan, we need you to tell us. Before it's too late.

9
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:48,060
Nothing would change if I did.

10
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:49,920
It might.

11
00:02:49,920 --> 00:03:01,060
I knew, and it didn't matter. Things happened. Things that can't be undone now. In the end, I wish I never knew anything.

12
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:08,700
If I knew about any of this, I would have tried to stop it from happening.

13
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,860
All we can do now is quit the Magius!

14
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:20,340
This is all wrong. If my friends are in danger, I don't want to be kept in the dark about it.

15
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:26,920
And if this is the end of everything, I want to be with them, not in a place like this.

16
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:32,300
Yeah, screw them, I guess. If Iroha and the others were in trouble, I should have known about it!

17
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:41,040
You're right. If only I had your courage, I could have chosen my fate, too.

18
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:44,440
What do you mean? Choose it now, it's not too late!

19
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:47,660
Yeah, totally. Come home with us if you want.

20
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:01,380
I can come with you?

21
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:04,000
Sure. Back to Mikazuki Villa.

22
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:08,500
We still need to find Tsuruno. I hope she's okay.

23
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:12,320
Don't worry, she's still alive.

24
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:14,760
That's a relief.

25
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,260
Oh, thank goodness.

26
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:21,460
After everything, I don't expect you to trust me. But if you do, leave Tsuruno to me.

27
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:27,400
I'll find her, and bring her back to Mikazuki Villa.

28
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:39,400
Iroha...

29
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:42,520
Ui! Where are you?

30
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:46,360
I'm over here. This way. Hurry!

31
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:47,320
Ui!

32
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:47,400
Ui!

33
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,320
Kurue...

34
00:04:53,320 --> 00:05:08,100
Hang on, Ui. I'll find you. But first, I have to find Nemu and Toka.

35
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:16,600
Ui!

36
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:42,460
There's so many witches. Why are they here?

37
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:45,460
Watch out!

38
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:50,500
Sorry about that!

39
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:52,620
I didn't hit you, did I?

40
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:57,100
She's okay, but I came close to having a heart attack.

41
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:00,820
Well, we meet again.

42
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:03,280
Yeah, and this time, I brought along some friends.

43
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:08,460
Okay...

44
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:10,960
Sorry, but that sounds totally crazy.

45
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:13,940
The Magius want witches to come to Kamehama?

46
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:20,780
Yes. And they convinced an army of magical girls of the plan, to make sure no one interfered with it.

47
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:23,620
How could they believe this is right?

48
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:24,340
How could they believe this is right?

49
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:25,620
They were tricked, of course.

50
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:32,900
The Magius say they're the key to our salvation, and as long as you're loyal to them, you won't turn into a witch.

51
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,460
You mean they can't do that?

52
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:36,240
You mean they can't do that? It's all just a lie?

53
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:40,660
Yes. A lie spread by girls who can't accept their fate.

54
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:46,180
The price we paid for our wishes can't be cancelled so easily.

55
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:52,520
Iroha, thank god.

56
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:54,760
Are you okay? Where are you?

57
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:57,840
I'm in Magius' theme park, on the teacup ride.

58
00:06:58,260 --> 00:06:58,640
Huh?

59
00:06:58,820 --> 00:07:00,860
I'm okay, they can't see me here.

60
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:02,920
But things are looking really bad.

61
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,340
More and more witches keep showing up.

62
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:08,060
The little Kyubei was with me, but he took off.

63
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,700
I got separated from Kuroi, too.

64
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,140
You're all alone, then?

65
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:15,180
Only for now. Kuroi said she'd catch up.

66
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:19,060
I can't wait much longer for her. I have to stop them.

67
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:21,980
Alright, stay put. I'll be there in a...

68
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:27,760
Iroha!

69
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:29,920
She was cut off.

70
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:32,540
Who's Iroha?

71
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:36,800
A friend. You saved us once before. She's the one in the hooded cloak.

72
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:38,740
Oh yeah, I'm glad she's safe.

73
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,100
She is, for now.

74
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:43,480
I have to get to her.

75
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:44,740
Hey, Sayaka.

76
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,400
Didn't you say you found Mami with the Magius?

77
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:48,560
Yeah.

78
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:51,700
Then if we help this girl out, maybe we'll find her.

79
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:52,580
What do you think?

80
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:53,520
Mm-hmm.

81
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:54,920
Yeah, Chiel.

82
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:56,960
Is it cool if we come with you?

83
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,440
That Mami friend of yours might be there.

84
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:01,620
She almost killed you last time.

85
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:03,460
Yeah, I know. I remember.

86
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:06,160
It's given me the chills just thinking about it.

87
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,380
So what?

88
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:09,280
We can't leave Mami with them.

89
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:10,280
They brainwashed her.

90
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:13,120
And if they're drying witches here, we can't ignore that.

91
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:15,220
We can deal with both at the same time.

92
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:18,440
If Miss Tomoe were in her right mind, she'd do the same.

93
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:22,260
All right. Thank you.

94
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:25,240
Now, let's end this nonsense.

95
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:40,280
You see that, Nemu?

96
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:42,940
All those souls were tiny little sparks.

97
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:46,380
And now, they're gonna set fire to the whole world.

98
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:54,100
I didn't know playing with fire was what the wings of the Magius were created for.

99
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:59,660
What's wrong? You don't look happy.

100
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:02,440
If something's bothering you, let's hear it.

101
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:07,660
Toka, I'm begging you, please stop the operation.

102
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:11,400
We're dragging innocent people into something they're not a part of.

103
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:15,240
You've always been so kind and considerate.

104
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,820
You see what's happening out there.

105
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:18,380
It's not too late to stop this.

106
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:23,360
Actually, Mifuyu, when you think about it, no one's really innocent.

107
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:26,620
Humanity wouldn't have advanced as far as it has.

108
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:29,420
If magical girls hadn't sacrificed their lives.

109
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:35,260
That all ends here.

110
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:40,660
I won't allow them to use us for the sake of their progress when they don't even know about us.

111
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:45,180
I'm begging you, please stop this.

112
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:49,080
You're having second thoughts about it, because you don't understand.

113
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,140
But that's okay.

114
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,440
That's where I come in.

115
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:52,860
I call the shots.

116
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:54,720
You don't have to understand.

117
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,440
Just follow my lead.

118
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:57,340
I will not!

119
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:59,140
This has to stop right now!

120
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:11,060
Suruno, I need your help!

121
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:25,560
Suruno, don't!

122
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:37,080
I'm sorry, Mifuyu.

123
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:44,280
Whatever time I had is almost up.

124
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:51,080
I was wondering, Toka...

125
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,240
About what?

126
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:58,600
When this is all over, can we go to that theme park?

127
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:00,820
Mm-hmm.

128
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:12,180
This isn't the place for playing games.

129
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:14,420
Vivo o morto, especially.

130
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,380
Mm-hmm.

131
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:17,780
Alina.

132
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:22,500
That's all you can say?

133
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:23,680
No grazie?

134
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,040
Oh well.

135
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:28,000
I'm leaving this hovel and going back to my artillery.

136
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,720
You're leaving?

137
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:36,380
I committed to Toka and Nemu's grandiose plans because I thought they had soul.

138
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:44,380
But ultimately my goal as an artiste wasn't having tea parties in castles with girls who have the intelligence of sheep.

139
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:49,340
Anywho, if you survive to the climax, do ring me up.

140
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,960
I'd love to know how this all played out.

141
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:53,760
Arrivederci!

142
00:11:53,760 --> 00:12:12,960
They got all the exits covered.

143
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:18,320
Hey.

144
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:21,160
I seen that girl before.

145
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:42,540
Are there any updates about this storm?

146
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:44,500
I'll check the weather.

147
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:45,860
Don't bother.

148
00:12:46,380 --> 00:12:47,580
I got your forecast here.

149
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:48,780
Ta-da!

150
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:50,620
Good thinking.

151
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:52,380
We'll have clear skies.

152
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:54,720
Huh?

153
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:59,280
Come on, hop in.

154
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:04,020
Does everyone have their seatbelts fastened?

155
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:05,520
Yes, ma'am.

156
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:10,940
The supercell is heading straight for the northeast, bringing heavy rain and gusty winds.

157
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:14,860
It's currently moving north along the Pacific coast and growing even stronger.

158
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:17,520
This is turning out to be the biggest storm.

159
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:26,100
I, um, I don't want to worry anyone, but do you think it's possible Valpurgus Doct will show up in Kamehama?

160
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,480
I never thought of that.

161
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:29,840
Why would you think she'd come here?

162
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:36,620
Well, um, we were told once that she would appear in Mitakihara City during a big storm.

163
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:42,860
Since the Magius are luring witches from all over to here, maybe they'd accidentally attract her, too.

164
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:46,100
At this point, I wouldn't rule anything out.

165
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:52,620
If they did lure Valpurgus not here, then everyone in Kamehama, including us, are doomed.

166
00:13:52,620 --> 00:14:11,680
Well, we shouldn't lose hope.

167
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:15,900
No matter how bad things look now, one of us could still save the day.

168
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:16,900
Yeah.

169
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:21,940
I know that as long as I have hope, I'll never regret being a magical girl.

170
00:14:27,740 --> 00:14:30,420
We all feel the same, I'm sure.

171
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:31,520
Big time.

172
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:35,080
Ours is not a bad fate.

173
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:36,520
Better change.

174
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,860
Things are going to get bumpy from here on.

175
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:39,720
Okay.

176
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:46,260
Are you two ready back there?

177
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:47,440
We're ready.

178
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,340
Hang on tight, then.

179
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:51,160
Time for some offensive driving.

180
00:14:58,120 --> 00:15:00,640
Wanna tell me what you think you're doing here?

181
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:01,040
Huh?

182
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:02,020
Oh, right.

183
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:05,200
I was just trying to get to that castle.

184
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,980
All by yourself?

185
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,680
That was the plan.

186
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:13,540
Someone has to stop them, and if I don't try, I know I'll regret it.

187
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:17,560
Yeah, well, you don't look tough enough to play the loner hero.

188
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:19,120
No offense or anything.

189
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:22,980
If they'd listen to anyone, I know they'd listen to me.

190
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:24,540
Why the heck would they?

191
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:26,240
Do you know those little brats or something?

192
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:28,500
Wait, did you talk to Nemo and the others?

193
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:31,340
Oh, no, I haven't.

194
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:35,760
I'm just telling it like it is and hoping this dumbass plan of theirs fails.

195
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:37,900
This isn't like them at all.

196
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:40,140
Something went wrong somewhere.

197
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:44,400
And I think if I can talk to them, maybe I can get them to stop.

198
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:48,120
That'll make it easier for you to get around.

199
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:49,760
Thanks, but like...

200
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:51,420
Who are you?

201
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:58,220
Hiroha Tamaki.

202
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:19,300
What a hit!

203
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:20,380
Indeed.

204
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:26,140
Miss Nanami!

205
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:26,260
Miss Nanami!

206
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,120
That was too close.

207
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:44,200
Thanks, Homura.

208
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,940
It was nothing.

209
00:16:46,340 --> 00:16:47,640
I'm glad you're both safe.

210
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:54,540
Now, we just have to figure out how to get in.

211
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:59,440
Everything seems to be going as we planned.

212
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,780
It's even better than we planned!

213
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:05,900
Iroha, can you hear me?

214
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:06,900
Iroha!

215
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:09,080
I hear you, Yachiyo.

216
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:10,020
Are you close?

217
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:11,800
Yes, I see the gate.

218
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:13,820
But getting through will be...

219
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:14,740
rather tricky.

220
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:20,160
Okay, hang on a sec.

221
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,160
I'll go and open it.

222
00:17:22,660 --> 00:17:24,220
Wait, it's too dangerous.

223
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,860
I'll find another way in.

224
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:28,620
I need your help, and this is our only chance!

225
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:30,360
Besides, I'm almost there.

226
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:31,600
I can handle this!

227
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:33,520
I'm the only one who can.

228
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:34,360
Trust me!

229
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:35,580
Okay.

230
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:38,340
Can she get it open by herself?

231
00:17:38,780 --> 00:17:41,000
Well, she sounded like she knew what she was doing.

232
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:43,200
She'll open it.

233
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:46,700
Open up the gate and hurry!

234
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:47,220
What?

235
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:49,680
No one gave us the order to open it.

236
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:50,840
I just gave it!

237
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:52,140
Please open up the gate!

238
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:54,080
Hurry up!

239
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:55,700
I said hurry up!

240
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:57,240
Yes, ma'am, right away.

241
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:03,180
I did it!

242
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:08,540
Irohatamaki!

243
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:09,960
Surrender now!

244
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:31,220
Now that was stupid!

245
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:32,380
What are you thinking?

246
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:34,280
I thought you left.

247
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:35,120
Surprise!

248
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:37,940
You won't live long taking risks like that.

249
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:40,640
Well, I'm not dead yet thanks to you.

250
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:43,760
You stayed to help, and I'm so grateful you did.

251
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:46,860
No time to get all mushy.

252
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:48,480
Come on, follow me.

253
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:50,720
Hey!

254
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:51,460
What are you doing?

255
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:52,340
We gotta go!

256
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:55,200
I became a magical girl in exchange for a wish,

257
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,220
just like you did.

258
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:57,580
I wanted this life!

259
00:18:58,160 --> 00:18:59,560
This is the path I chose,

260
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:01,420
and I can't waste that wish!

261
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,800
I don't know what you wished for,

262
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,380
but after hearing all that,

263
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:08,260
I'd say it was an early grave.

